.TH "ROOT" 7 "February 2026" "atomdns handlers" "atomdns authors"

.SH "NAME"
.PP
\fIroot\fP \- override the global root

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Usually the global section has a \fB\fCroot\fR directive. This handler allows you to override it for each handler
block if desired. It works identical to the atomdns\-global(1) root's configuration.

.SH "SYNTAX"
.PP
.RS

.nf
root DIRECTORY

.fi
.RE

.IP \(bu 4
with \fB\fCroot\fR \fBDIRECTORY\fP is the directory to use as the root directory for the server. Any relative path
names will get this directory prefixed. If \fBDIRECTORY\fP itself is also relative the current working
directory (cwd) of the atomdns process will be prefixed.


.SH "NOTES"
.PP
This handler must be set first in a handler block to effect all handlers in the block.
